@cc ===========================================================================
@cc CHATVT:MODE - build the offline SERVER-SEND test.
@cc
@cc   @MODE CHATVT:MODE,,
@cc then          @CHATVT
@cc
@cc Links the REAL CHATSV:BRF, so CHATSV must have been compiled first with
@cc its EXPORT block (@MODE CHATSV:MODE,,). CHATLIB supplies the kinds and
@cc the cm* frame readers the checks decode with.
@cc ===========================================================================

@cc --- clear the old build; NO SUCH FILE NAME on a first run is expected -----
@DELETE-FILE CHATVT:PROG
@DELETE-FILE CHATVT:BRF
@DELETE-FILE CHATVT:LIST

@cc --- compile to a real BRF; PROG-FILE NOT set, on purpose -------------------
@PLANC-100-F00
COMPILE CHATVT:PLNC,"CHATVT:LIST","CHATVT"
EXIT

@cc --- link: the test first, then the server it drives, then the libraries ---
@BRF-LINKER-C01
PROGRAM-FILE "CHATVT"
LOAD CHATVT
LOAD CHATSV
LOAD CHATLIB
LIBRARY-MODE ON
LOAD XMP-100-1-B02
LOAD MON-CALL-1B-A00
LOAD PLANC-1BANK-F00
LIST-ENTRIES-UNDEFINED
EXIT

@cc ===========================================================================
@cc Built CHATVT:PROG. Run it with @CHATVT - needs XMSG up on this machine.
@cc
@cc Every line starts PASS or FAIL and the last line is a count. Part A is
@cc buildFromSlot, part B is broadcast's audience, part C is three rounds
@cc whose content must follow the round - the live bug's exact shape.
@cc
@cc CHECK BOTH LISTINGS (CHATVT:LIST and the CHATSV:LIST this links against)
@cc for "*** ERROR" before believing any of it.
@cc ===========================================================================
